        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test(infra): add unit tests for executable token normalization",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `exec-wrapper-tokens.ts` module normalizes executable tokens for wrapper and policy matching, handling cross-platform path differences and Windows executable suffixes. Without tests, the normalization logic could silently regress.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd unit tests for `basenameLower` and `normalizeExecutableToken` covering POSIX paths, Windows paths, suffix stripping (.exe/.cmd/.bat/.com), non-executable extensions, and edge cases.\n\n## User Impact\n\nExecutable token normalization now has comprehensive test coverage, reducing regression risk.\n\n## Evidence\n\nDirect behavior probe with real function calls:\n\n```text\n$ node --import tsx -e \"import('./src/infra/exec-wrapper-tokens.js').then(({basenameLower,normalizeExecutableToken})=>console.log(JSON.stringify([{f:'basenameLower',i:'/usr/bin/Node',r:basenameLower('/usr/bin/Node')},{f:'normalizeExecutableToken',i:'node.exe',r:normalizeExecutableToken('node.exe')},{f:'normalizeExecutableToken',i:'C:\\Program Files\\node.exe',r:normalizeExecutableToken('C:\\Program Files\\node.exe')}])))\"\n[{\"f\":\"basenameLower\",\"i\":\"/usr/bin/Node\",\"r\":\"node\"},{\"f\":\"normalizeExecutableToken\",\"i\":\"node.exe\",\"r\":\"node\"},{\"f\":\"normalizeExecutableToken\",\"i\":\"C:\\Program Files\\node.exe\",\"r\":\"node\"}]\n```\n\nTargeted test:\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run src/infra/exec-wrapper-tokens.test.ts\n\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  9 passed (9)\n  Duration  385ms\n```\n\nFormatting:\n\n```text\n$ npx oxfmt --check src/infra/exec-wrapper-tokens.ts src/infra/exec-wrapper-tokens.test.ts\nChecking formatting...\n\nAll matched files use the correct format.\nFinished in 114ms on 2 files using 8 threads.\n```\n\nWhitespace:\n\n```text\n$ git diff --check\n```",
